WEBVTT

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.870
Space--the final tourist spot.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.700
There, we'll no doubt find epicurean
feats to stagger the imagination

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.660
and entirely new activities waiting for us!

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.080
"Hamama II, home of eel-based virility"
"At last, a close encounter with Yang!"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.410
"Not sure what kind of anime this is anymore (heh)"
"Qu-eel-le Surprise"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.950
"Not sure what kind of anime this is anymore (heh)"
"Qu-eel-le Surprise"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.330
Planet number 29 on the Galaxy Highway,

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:55.370
Hamama II!

00:01:55.370 --> 00:02:00.250
Hamama II is a kingdom.
It says it's famous for its eel.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.700
Is eel really that good?

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.910
Ugh, is this what's become
of your generation?

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.950
Ever since commerce treaties
with aliens fell through

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.700
and they were overfished by the Totchinans,

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.250
we haven't been able to catch
any eel back on Earth.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.950
Oh, now you're citing
generational differences?

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.580
What, are you trying to call me old?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.000
Not really. Sure, our generation
is only familiar with

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:23.500
"Rice with eel glaze"
"Rice with eel-flavored flakes"
Not really. Sure, our generation
is only familiar with

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.700
"Rice with eel glaze"
"Rice with eel-flavored flakes"
the taste of eel glaze and
eel-flavored flakes for our rice.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.870
Those are pretty good for what
they are, but I feel bad for you.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:36.910
Imagine, never having
eaten actual grilled eel...

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:44.250
Once we get to Hamama II,
I'll show you how to eat true eel.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.500
I appreciate your guidance.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:51.830
Ah, lucky us! Hamama II's
Great Eel Festival starts today!

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:56.950
Oh, how exciting! The Great Eel Festival!

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.700
My generation wouldn't take these
for eels under any circumstances.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.580
From where I sit, these look like oxen.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.620
There's no "Great," "Eel," or
"Festival" anywhere to be had!

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:23.290
Um, excuse me...

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.250
Hmm?

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.750
Awesome! You're so buff!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.580
This is no time for you to admire him!

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:33.160
Oh, right. About this Great Eel Festival...

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.250
Eel!

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:39.250
--Um, about this Great Eel Festival...
--Eel! Eel! Eel!

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:40.620
--Eel!
--Eel!

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.500
Eel!

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.290
The festival begins!

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:49.450
--Eel! Eel! Eel!
--Eel! Eel! Eel!

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.790
This is more of a cattle drive festival, huh?

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.160
Maybe they've confused this
for the Day of the Ox?

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.540
We'll get to chow down on steak.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.000
Are they using eel sauce?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.160
I wonder if it's any good.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.500
This is perfect for a challenge-minded
fellow like yourself, isn't it?

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.910
I'm gonna opt out, though.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.370
What does that mean?

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.500
--Eel!
--What the...?

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:13.950
It's a monster!

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.120
A dinosaur!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.830
It's a giant eel!

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.080
<i>That's </i>an eel?!

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.830
Eels sure are big, aren't they?

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:27.410
That's <i>too </i>big! It's swallowing
those oxen whole!

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.290
Eel!

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.660
Being chased by a giant eel is not
something you get to do very often.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.700
I don't wanna! What kind of festival is this?!

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.580
It's the Hamama II Great Eel Festival!

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.450
I know that!

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:51.830
Eel! Eel! Eel!

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:56.660
Eel!

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.950
Amazing. This is like a tuna-fileting show.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.870
--Tuna?
--You don't know what tuna is, either?!
You know what? Never mind.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.870
Explaining everything to you
is becoming a pain.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.620
What is this?

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.540
We have mechas and spaceships,
so why do they risk their lives like this?

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.830
Oh, you know, no matter
how far civilization advances,

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.330
we still hold on to our
traditions from the past.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:26.580
Superstitions, inhibitions,
claims to the throne, and stuff like that.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.830
Fellows!

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:32.450
You are brave to take part in the
Great Eel Festival from the start,

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.080
being tourists as you are.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.910
It's not bravery! We just
didn't know what this was!

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:41.450
You don't normally think the
"great" in "Great Eel Festival"

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:42.950
refers to the <i>eel</i>!

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:43.410
"Great Eel Festival"
"Great Eel"
"Great Festival"
refers to the <i>eel</i>!

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.500
"Great Eel Festival"
"Great Eel"
"Great Festival"
Normally, the "great" refers to the <i>festival</i>.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.040
Yeah, I guess. What do you say
about hiring me as your guide?

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:51.870
Guide?

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.950
We don't need a guide! If you were
a young lady, that would be one thing,

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.700
but you're still just a child, aren't you?

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:02.500
Oh, don't say that, mister.
The truth is, in last year's festival,

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.540
my daddy was swallowed by a great eel.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:05.620
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.500
He was swallowed?

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:08.040
Your daddy?

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.830
Mm-hmm.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:13.950
I see. So you've been hard up ever since
and offered to be our guide?

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.580
That about covers it.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.000
Okay, you got it.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:17.660
Huh?!

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.410
Hooray!

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:20.750
I'm Unami.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:25.330
Misters, you should change into
Great Eel Festival costumes right away.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.290
You mean "fellows," right?

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:31.290
Okay, "fellows," let's go!

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.250
She's nice and accommodating.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.330
Mr. Yang, we're at Hamama II.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:43.370
And you're sure that Robby
is down on this planet, right?

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.700
Yes, sir, no doubt about it.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:49.660
Ah! Mr. Yang, Mr. Yang!
The Great Eel Festival is underway!

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:53.040
It looks like there's
all-you-can-eat grilled eel and so on!

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.450
Great Eel Festival, eh?

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:02.910
Fortifying my virility before catching
Robby might not be a bad idea.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.540
Grilled Hamama eel!

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.330
Hey, that's huge!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.910
Let's eat, let's eat!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.200
Don't waste our money.
One skewer is 2000 mons!

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.660
These are 2000 mons? No way!

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.120
Two skewers are 4000 mons!

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.120
Yum!

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.000
Is this the true flavor of eel?

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:35.160
Yeah! As good as Earth's! And even
better than the sad farmed kind.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.750
It's what Hamama II is known for, after all.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:39.790
Be careful not to overhunt them.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:43.660
Not to worry. Our king is keeping
the generational tradition.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:44.830
No doubt.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:48.410
The "Touch the Eel" event
is starting in the west arena.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.620
I don't wanna touch them!

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.410
They're slimy and squishy and mucky,
and feel great, though.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.750
Even I am going to have to turn that down.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.330
The eel catching event is
happening in the east arena.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.950
You can't catch them!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.950
They're just babies, so you can.
There's even prize money.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.580
Did you say prize money?

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:07.290
Mm-hmm. Prize money from the king
is awarded depending on how you do.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:11.450
Go! Compete and bring back
that prize money, you deadbeats!

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:16.250
Catching baby eels, huh?
Okay, I'll give it a shot!

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:21.790
Ha-ha, looks like he messed that up.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:24.410
I am never doing that.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:27.950
This is quite a nice festival, isn't it?

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.290
Mr. Yang!

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.080
I bought you an eel bone!

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:33.450
It's huge!

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.450
Hmph.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:45.580
Oh, that hits the spot!

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:53.330
That gets the old engine running!

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:56.750
Mr. Yang, they're selling
disgusting eel liver over there!

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:00.910
Go buy me some! I'm going
to get my engine running!

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:07.660
<i>Seiya</i>! <i>Seiya</i>! <i>Seiya</i>! <i>Seiya</i>!

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.580
An eel palanquin, huh?

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.870
I bought you some gross grilled liver!

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.540
Oh, that's the stuff!

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:30.750
Festivals are fun!

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:34.620
Yeah. It makes you forget
about the melancholy of life!

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:40.330
Robby! Wherever you are,
I'm going to catch you!

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:49.000
The most popular hotel among tourists
is the Unazuki. The Hotel Unazuki.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.370
Then we're going to stay the night here.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.540
Hooray!

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:56.080
There's an eel rodeo race tomorrow.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.790
Rodeo? You mean,
people ride those giant eels?

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.500
They put saddles on them, so it's okay.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.750
Is it really okay, though?

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:02.910
--Beats me.
--Beats me.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.830
They award prize money,
so remember me when you tip.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.540
Prize money?!

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.500
--Enter it, you two! And win!
You got that, you two?!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.620
--Okay, see you tomorrow.
--Enter it, you two! And win!
You got that, you two?!

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.580
No reservation, room please.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.500
Is it the three of you?

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:23.330
Negative. I am a mascot toy. Whrr.

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:25.160
So it's just the two of us.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:29.290
We have regular, deluxe, and supreme
suites. Which would you like?

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.540
Let's treat ourselves with the supreme--

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.200
Regular! Regular! Regular! Regular! Whrr.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.910
Will two singles be all right?

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:36.830
No problem.

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:39.910
Which room will the mascot toy go in?

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:45.370
What?! I just pretended to be
a toy to get a lower room rate!

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.750
And just so you know,
this is every last mon we have!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.120
--If you want to continue this journey,
you have to win the prize tomorrow!

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:53.870
--It says supper is a wall-to-wall
eel buffet in the main dining room.
--If you want to continue this journey,
you have to win the prize tomorrow!

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:57.200
Yes! Let's take a short break
and reconvene for the buffet!

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.120
Mm-hmm.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.410
Hey! Stop ignoring me!

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:01.790
Ikku, hurry!

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:04.200
Tch, what's the use? I'm coming.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:05.750
Okay, see you later.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:17.290
Robby! Where the hell
did you go? Where are you?

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:24.250
Hmm, this fried eel fin
is getting the job done!

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:27.410
Mr. Yang, maybe you're
over-fortifying yourself?

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:32.500
I have to be able to reach my
maximum power when I find Robby!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.330
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.160
How come?

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.910
Beats me.

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:39.660
Mr. Yang, this is the most
popular hotel among tourists.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:42.250
Do you have any lodgers from Earth?

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:44.910
We have a great deal of guests from there.

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:47.410
It's the Great Eel Festival, after all.

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:49.290
Any who look like this?

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:53.040
Well, um, Earthlings all look the same to me.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.040
Enough! Get me a room!

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.370
--We have regular, deluxe, and supreme--

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.870
--Supreme! And throw in some eel liver soup!
--We have regular, deluxe, and supreme--

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.950
Whole-grilled eel!

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.750
Let's see here...

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:06.120
Hey, this is good!

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:11.410
Broiled eel, eel liver soup, eel gratin,
eel steak, eel curry, eel pie...

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:15.290
Eat whatever you feel like.
I had it a lot when I was a kid.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.620
Ah, I found eel jello!

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:19.080
Eel jello?

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:25.120
Hmm, never tasted this before. I don't like it.

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.660
You don't? It's good.

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:33.160
I'll take a nice, simple eel broil.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.410
Not that it matters, but ever since we arrived,

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:37.290
I haven't seen any Hamaman beauties.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:40.160
Now that you mention it,
they're all musclebound men, huh?

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.080
The Eel Festival dance show
will now be held in the main hall.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:48.370
A dance show?! Hamaman beauties,
for the first time since we got here!

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.540
Woo-hoo! Let's go!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.540
Don't go flying off the handle!

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.330
Robby...

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.040
Mr. Yang, take it easy!

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.410
We'll find Robby!

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:04.910
Robby...

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:07.620
Robby...!

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:15.450
Aw, there goes Mr. Yang
again, over-fortifying.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:20.620
--Eel! Eel!
--Eel! Eel!

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.410
Why is it all guys?

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:23.540
Take that.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.450
I'm going to bed.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.410
I'm going to go look around some more.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.250
I'm curious about the electric eel baths.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:32.700
Don't go getting eaten.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.200
You, either.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:39.620
So sleepy...

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.000
Robby!

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:46.040
Whoa, who are you?

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:49.660
Robby!

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:51.250
Mr. Yang, no!

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:53.580
Robby isn't here!

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.790
It tingles, it tingles!
Th-Th-This electric eel bath is terrific!

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.870
Ow-w-w... It stings, but it's terrific!

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:06.950
You really do like experiencing the
strangest things. Are you a masochist?

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:10.410
I-I-I don't even know, myself!

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:12.450
"Pray at the Isekandar Temple"

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.410
"Pray at the Isekandar Temple"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.410
"Go shopping on Okage Street"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:21.870
"Get Akafucrystals as gifts"
♪ Isekan is a great place! ♪

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:25.120
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:27.450
"Act now and this Isekandar bag is included!!"
♪ Come on, let's go! ♪

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:38.830
Pretty girls... Pretty girls...

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:41.290
Hey, why don't you get to sleep already?

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:43.450
You have to win that prize money tomorrow.

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:44.950
You're right.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:50.250
What? Did you just hear someone's voice?

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.410
Yeah, I did.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:14.540
I can't eat anymore...

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:17.950
RRR-obby...!

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.450
It's coming...

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:21.540
...this way...

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:27.500
It's right outside...

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:49.790
Robby!

00:15:55.830 --> 00:16:00.500
What was I just...? I should go to bed.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.910
What... just happened?

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.500
Is this...

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:14.660
...blood?

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.450
Must have been some kind of incident.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.370
A g-g-ghost...

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.200
--Huh?
--A spirit!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:23.620
--Huh?
--Ooh, I'm scared!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:27.330
It's the ghost of a Hamaman that
was eaten by an eel, I just know it!

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:32.200
I took you to be pretty down-to-earth,
but you're afraid of ghosts.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.200
Events that can't be explained by science

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.500
are way mysterious and scary, right?

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:38.950
Ah, so that's your type.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:40.910
There, there.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:47.500
Good morning!

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.500
Hey.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.080
Good morning...

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:52.700
What would you like to do about
winning prize money today?

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.750
I didn't get enough sleep, so I'll pass.

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.370
I'm entering the race!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.120
Okay, we'll go to the main stadium
where they're holding the races.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:00.200
Roger!

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:14.330
They said I could pick whichever one
I liked, but which one should I pick?

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:15.830
This one looks pretty tasty.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.950
Choose one that looks light on its feet.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.450
They don't have feet.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:22.500
If you win, you'll get a commendation
from the king himself!

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:24.950
You'll be a hero!

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:29.000
A hero, huh? That should
make me pretty popular.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.450
You're drooling.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:39.000
There are prizes up to third place.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:43.580
They said this was the biggest
event of the eel festival.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.080
Do you think Robby is here?

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.870
Even if he is, we'll never find him like this.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.790
Where is Robby?!

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:53.620
Aw, Mr. Yang is over-fortifying himself again.

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:56.040
Yahoo!

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:58.250
This is a lively one!

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.700
Looking cool!

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.500
Don't get bucked off!

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:03.870
I found you!

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:05.750
Robby!

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:09.000
Huh? Is that you, Yang?
What are you doing here?

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.580
Did he actually chase us
outside of the galaxy?

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:12.830
That's right!

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.120
Don't ever underestimate Mr. Yang!

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:16.910
Move!

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:20.160
Pay me back what you owe, Robby!

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.500
I have absolutely nothing on me right now,

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.910
so I'll pay you back once I return to Earth.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:29.040
Your account is still in arrears! Arrears!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.160
Huh?

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:33.620
Give me what you owe me!
Plus the interest on your debt!

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:35.250
I need you to pay interest!

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.870
I'll settle up once I get back to Earth.

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:40.450
Your debt, with interest! Right now!

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:47.370
Let the main race of the Great Eel Festival,
the Nurumite Cup, now starts!

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.120
Run! I mean, crawl! Get us out of here!

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:52.290
Wait the hell up, Robby!

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.580
Pay your interest!

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:56.000
I can't pay you a single mon right now!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:59.200
<i>Rishi</i>-<i>rishi</i>-<i>rishi</i>-<i>rishi</i>-<i>shi</i>-<i>ri</i>!
[rishi: "interest"]

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.080
<i>Shiri</i>?
[shiri: "butt"]

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.290
Pay your bill!

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.290
I'm telling, you, I don't have a single mon!

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:06.450
<i>Tsuke</i>-<i>tsuke</i>-<i>tsuke</i>-<i>tsuke</i>-<i>ke</i>-<i>tsu</i>!
[tsuke: "bill"]

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:07.120
<i>Ketsu</i>?
[ketsu: "ass"]

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.000
Butt!

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.410
I don't understand!

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:12.950
Ass!

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:16.830
No! Stop!

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:18.450
Ass!

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:19.870
--Mr. Yang!
--Mr. Yang!

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:21.250
--Robby!
--Robby!

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:25.000
Two racers have pulled away from the pack!
Two racers have taken the lead!

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:26.120
--They are rapidly breaking away!
Rapidly breaking away!

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.080
--<i>Rishi</i>-<i>tsuke</i>-<i>ketsu</i>-<i>shiri</i>!
--They are rapidly breaking away!
Rapidly breaking away!

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:31.040
--Is that a palindrome?!
--They're rounding the last corner
and into the last straightaway!

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:34.000
--<i>Rishi</i>-<i>tsuke</i>-<i>ketsu</i>-<i>shiri</i>!
--It's entirely down to these two!
Inside racer? Outside racer?

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:34.750
--<i>Rishi</i>-<i>tsuke</i>-<i>ketsu</i>-<i>shiri</i>!
--Which will it be? Which will it be?

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:35.000
--No!
--Which will it be? Which will it be?

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.160
--No!
--The outside racer pulls ahead!

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:41.620
They reach the goal! This year's
winning eel has been decided!

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:44.200
The winner is Number 5, paying 12-5.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:45.540
--Robby--
--Eel!

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.450
--Hey, where are you taking me?!
--Eel!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.870
The award ceremony, the award ceremony!

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:50.830
Eel!

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:51.790
What?

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.290
--Eel! Eel!
--Eel! Eel!

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:55.160
Eel?

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.370
Eel!

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.080
What do you mean, "eel"?

00:19:58.080 --> 00:19:58.910
Yang!

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.160
--Yang?
--Yang?

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:01.160
Yang!

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:02.580
--Yang?
--Yang?

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:03.580
Eel!

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.080
Yang!

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.700
Mr. Yang! When in Rome, do as the Romans!

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:09.370
And here, it's "eel"!

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:12.330
Eel!

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:15.040
Shut up! I'm Yang!

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.160
Yang!

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.290
Eel!

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:20.000
Yang!

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.410
I got the prize money for coming in second.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:27.290
Unami, here's your tip.

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.790
This much, really?

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:31.410
Thanks! My daddy will be thrilled!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.500
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:35.000
I thought your daddy
was swallowed by an eel.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.250
Is he all right?

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:39.870
Mm-hmm. He got swallowed,
but he broke through the eel's belly,

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:41.750
and ended up killing the eel, instead.

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:43.450
Eel!!

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:45.200
--What the hell?!
--What the hell?!

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:48.660
Aw, I wanted to be the hero and get the girls.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:52.580
Speaking of which, I haven't seen any
Hamaman girls except for you, Unami.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:54.040
Now that you mention it...

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.950
What are you talking about? I'm a boy, too.

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.330
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.910
Hamamans only have males.

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.040
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:11.000
I never thought Mr. Yang would come
all the way to Hamama II to collect a debt.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:15.450
Robby's debt is 20 million mons, right?
Isn't that a little inefficient?

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:17.000
Did he say anything to you?

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.370
Huh? Uh...

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:22.120
Hmm, not especially...

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:24.160
Ass-butt!

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.950
Anyhow, we have to flee
to the next stage station world!

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:32.040
Space runaway!

00:23:09.330 --> 00:23:12.410
Robby ran away on us, huh?

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:13.250
Yeah.

00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:15.870
Are you sure you don't
want to hurry after him?

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:19.540
We will. But my feelings...

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:22.160
--Feelings?
--What feelings are those?

00:23:22.160 --> 00:23:25.330
What I'm going to do after I catch Robby.

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:27.830
Obviously, you're going to
collect his debt, aren't you?

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:29.910
You said you'd take it out of his hide!

00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:31.790
Y-Yeah...

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:33.870
You're going to put him on a tuna boat, right?

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:35.580
No, you'll sell his kidneys!

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:36.540
It's not that.

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:38.410
Then what is it?

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:42.500
Well, it's, um...

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:43.540
Huh?

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:45.160
Mr. Yang?

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:52.790
"Next time"
"#07 'Land of Dreams Just Ahead'"

00:23:52.790 --> 00:23:56.950
"Next time"
"#07 'Land of Dreams Just Ahead'"
Next time, "Land of Dreams Just Ahead."

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:01.950
"Akka Sakka, the planet of love and hope"
"Pure! Right! Amusing!"

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:06.950
"A once-per-year starry night"
"Who will be the one to ring the bell?!"
